.alert.alert-light.border.mb-0
  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Goal of this page
  %p.mb-3
    Establish a shared baseline of ability milestones once: you and the other participant each rate privately per ability, then talk with ratings revealed when both have rated that ability, then award. After that, milestones move only when demonstrated—no full re-calibration.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Context
  = render 'shared/maap/definition'

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Specifics of this page
  %ul.mb-0
    %li
      %strong Select to save
      — choosing 1–5 saves immediately. First answer and any later change are both timestamped (cannot clear back to unanswered).
    %li
      %strong Ready for review per ability
      — when both of you have rated an ability (1–5), that ability shows both proposals so you can talk and award.
    %li
      %strong Audit trail
      — under the status pills you’ll see each person’s first selection and last change (value + time), so changing after seeing the other answer is visible.
    %li
      %strong M0 = not answered
      — proposal ratings are 1–5 only.
    %li
      Prefer this ritual over bulk award when establishing a baseline. Bulk award remains for edge cases only.
